{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413239-brainstorming-sample-plots-for-20th-mta","id":1413239,"title":"Brainstorming - Sample Plots for 20th MtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-12T08:51:15-07:00","id":1413239,"title":"Brainstorming - Sample Plots for 20th MtA","content":"This is a brainstorming exercise. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What are some decent, maybe good, sample starter plot for <i>Mage the Ascension 20th</i>? Specifically, one for a group of new players, ones who are mostly unfamiliar with the setting and the rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> There is a lot of material for MtA 20th, but it can be too much for a new group. I'm not new to the material, but players may be. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T13:40:00-07:00","id":1413273,"title":"","content":"From my experience there are some for Orphans and three for a tradition group.<br /> <br /> 1. The tradition group is, that your characters are a bunch of newly awakened characters and one oracle ordered, that it is important that those initiands work together despite not of the same tradition.<br /> <br /> 2. Your characters are members of a band and suddenly one strange monk appears and telling them, that god blessed their voice and talent and they should use their gift for<br /> <br /> 3. After a wild party with many drugs your characters started to see things. While they want to go to the party to either sue the guy for overdosing them with LSD or trying to get a cure, it turns out, that there hallucinations are more real then they thought. Now they need to go down the rabbit hole to regain control over their senses and getting sure again, what is just a missinterpration because of chemical violation and what is real real.<br /> <br /> And here for orphans.<br /> <br /> First your characters have strange dreams, hear voices, etc and go to a therapist. The therapist turns out the be a mage that is doing this job trying to find those mages that are unknown of their gift and teach them, that they are not crazy but in for a more mindintensiv therapy.<br /> <br /> Second your characters are part of the neighbourhood where two packs of werewolves attacked each other. Afterwards the characters are the only ones that can remember to it and because the rest either denied it happened, just said it whas a dream or something else, they go invasting and find each other where each other can assure, that it is not their mind going crazy for not denying like the rest, that it really happened. On the later invastigation they find a shaman that is living with them but because those characters are not part of the family whatever this means (neither player nor characters should know about kinfolk) the shaman teaches them about Gaia seperatly away from the pack because the Werewolves do not like it if outsiders see and know of them.<br /> <br /> Third the characters are part of an accident, terrorist attack, crazy gun shooter, whatever is dangerous, should kill them is better not radiactive but survive it like a wonder and mayby even mostly unharmed. The characters are soon contacted by a man that got known about it and tell them, they used instinctive magic and he will teach them to use this power.<br /> <br /> Fourth each of the characters has a high regarded person of them in a cult. The cult leader offers them to let them go after they are part of one session and still call him a liar.<br /> There it not only turned out he uses real magic but they can use them too and so joined him because he opened their eyes.<br /> <br /> Fifth the characters are part of the city where a sabbath elder tries to get the camerilla vampires killed by getting the SI on the trails with him randomly draining persons and embracing them so that the masquerade breach get spread. Each of the characters has a beloved person turned into this and while searching for a cure or someone to teach them how to live with it they are found by a mage with a tremere partner/spouse who search for the vampire endangering all of them. Like a turn of fate or god the characters awakened too and now the mage will teach them and let the tremere teach their beloved how to be cainite with a possibility on letting him help hunting this vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T14:27:41-07:00","id":1413442,"title":"","content":"A rare/unique and powerful (level 5+) Talisman/artifact has turned up in the city. Please try to find it. <br /> <br /> The local cultural center (that also doubles as a youth center and community hub) is in danger of being closed down, possibly for mundane reasons but also possibly as part of a Technocratic plot. Please save it.<br /> <br /> A wave of spiritual possessions is sweeping the area. Please investigate. <br /> <br /> A serial killer is operating in the city and their actions appear to be part of some sort of Infernalist/Nephandic ritual. Please help stop it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T21:08:24-07:00","id":1413490,"title":"","content":"We kind of already had a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067534-1000-mage-plots\">Mage Plotlines thread</a> going, albeit it's been unused for a while. But whatever, let's roll with this.<br /> <hr />A small time art gallery has just been robbed. The trick - the thing that actually attracted the attention of the PCs in the first place - is that while one painting was stolen, every other painting had its &quot;occupants&quot; go missing from their frames at the same time. (Ex: Where once was a portrait, now only the background remains; where once was a group shot of people in a field is now just a field). The curator is unable to get the police to investigate the theft seriously (because their track record for finding stolen goods is positively stellar), so there's only lazy beat cop hanging around the gallery, pretending to look at evidence. The PCs need to not only get around the cop (and possibly the curator, who may need to be convinced to let them help) to get clues (physical, spiritual, anything in the gallery records or security cameras, etc), and track down the thief, but wrangle all the painted people now wandering around the city. They have three days before the Technocracy catches wind of the event and starts dealing with the Reality Deviance their own way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Newly Awakened and as-yet unaffiliated PCs all show up at a new age bookstore, as if by coincidence, fate, someone's plan, or the urging of their Avatars. All seek answers about the power they've gained. Also by coincidence, fate, or design, the bookstore owner is a Mage who has fallen under the radar of a gang of amateur witch-hunters. The PCs are caught in the crossfire, and must sneak, bluff, persuade, intimidate, or blast their way out of this sticky situation. All while potentially saving the lives of the store owner, and whatever hapless Sleepers happen to be in the store at the time. Or they could just leave them to die, though this may come back to bite them later...<br /> <br /> <br /> NPCs associated with the PCs' Backgrounds or pasts have been kidnapped by a small organized crime outfit (either a gang or small time mobster). Their leader - probably due to some shadowy figures pulling the strings - knows the PCs have power, and so is using their kidnapped associates/loved ones as leverage to get the PCs to help with a problem. That problem: a rival gang has absconded with some of the crime outfit's property (a sizable drug shipment, high explosives, some illegal firearms, or the like), and the leader wants the PCs to get it back for them. How the PCs go about this is up to them, the leader doesn't care. They could sneak in, intimidate the rivals, destroy or otherwise subdue them with outright force or subterfuge, even negotiate a return of goods. The leader is also not opposed to having replacements of those stolen goods, or even an equivalent amount of money. Despite being a criminal, the crime outfit's leader is good as his word. He's ballsy enough to strong-arm some baby wizards into helping him, but savvy enough to know not to go back on his word or kill the hostages. He's superstitious enough to know not to piss off wizards who could, if not now, then one day in the future become powerful enough to make his life miserable and short. On the other hand, the PCs could always dispense with playing by the outfit's rules, and rescue the hostages directly, and/or kill/eliminate the outfit.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the players all invested in a Chantry, their first mission involves securing it. A Node has just become available, though possibly a weak one, and the PCs are sent by their Traditions/Craft(s) to claim it for their respective side of the Ascension War. Of course, it's not as empty as they were led to believe. Maybe there are a bunch of homeless squatters, who won't want to leave without recompense or &quot;motivation&quot;; assuming the PCs don't decide to try to convert the squatters to their side. Or some kind of Bygone may be dwelling near the Node itself, sustaining itself on the Quintessence (and on whatever people may be in the vicinity). It might be both, with the squatters living in fear of a monster that is preying upon them, but having no other place to go. A ghost is always a classic option, and it may be as hostile and difficult to oust/resolve as the ST desires. After the place is secured, the PCs may wish to find a way to acquire the property in a legal sense, if they don't want to just become squatters themselves. In addition, there may be interference from neighbors, such as a home owner's association, fundamentalist church, or simply nosy people. Whoever they are, they have a distrustful attitude towards hipsters, vagrants, new agers, or &quot;criminal-looking types&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T21:38:41-07:00","id":1413493,"title":"","content":"Something is going around the local dives, finding the saddest person in the bar and draining them of their essence and leaving behind sometimes literally the husk of a human. This has noticeably drawn attention from groups the local awakened community would rather have not wanted poking around in their affairs to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T06:35:52-07:00","id":1413553,"title":"","content":"The player group stumble on witnesses of events that involved a group noticeably similar to them. They investigate further and see pictures and even video recordings showing what appears to be figures that look like then with one member different and some of the others say missing an arm or eye or with a mystical prosthetic. They eventually meet with their doubles and it seems at some point in each PCs training as an apprentice Mage they entered either the spirit world, a chantry or a portal and two of them appeared on the other end. They appear to be alternate versions of the PC group with different life experiences after the duplication event to the point where some of the these doubles are different traditions/crafts/conventions. They have slightly different Foci and one of them has a different body due to either a paradox backlash or a purposeful permanent shaping/curse. But one member of the group seems to be exactly the same as their double, why are they a constant? For poignancy have the constant one be a member that is particularly virtuous or the most scoundrel like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T12:28:24-07:00","id":1413603,"title":"","content":"<i><u>Weighing the Cost</u></i> introduces the problems of the power of magic and is a pretty lightweight story. Jamie McAlester needs some stats, but other than that, you could easily run it for new mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}